From f9ab2faf3e292983033d80d9804976ef915676f8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julien Etienne <julien.etienne@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 17:11:40 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt6797: build the mac80211 layer as a loadable module

MT6797_MAC80211 becomes tristate. Built in, nothing changes: the CONSYS
owner starts the firmware and attaches the mac80211 layer in the same
work as before (private record, registration, the initial TC4
accounting pair, scan ready), now through mt6797_consys_wlan_attach().

As a module (mac), the CONSYS owner still starts the firmware at boot,
keeps the started HIF and its capability, and logs that the module
attaches on load. Loading mac runs the same attach once. A second attach,
or one before the firmware is ready, is refused; a failed attach is not
retried, since it may leave firmware state behind. There is no detach
yet, so the module has no exit and stays loaded.

The module keeps the name mac, so its parameters stay under
/sys/module/mac/parameters. Its debugfs helpers (snapshot, testcfg) stay
built in, and the HIF, record, snapshot and testcfg functions it calls
are exported GPL-only.
